Say which of the call gate's guards rejected a decrypt-append.

DIAGNOSTIC PATCH, off unless -DPORT_SE_CRYPTO_TRACE is passed
(CRYPTO_TRACE=1 in the Makefile).  It adds printf calls and changes no
logic.

SE_CallGateService's SE_CRYPTO_LL_DECRYPT_APPEND_ID case runs its guards
twice each -- ST repeats them deliberately, as a fault-injection
countermeasure -- and each one fails identically: assign SE_ERROR, break.
peSE_Status has already been set to SE_OK by then, so a caller that gets
SE_ERROR with status SE_OK knows only that SOME guard fired.

The symptom this was written for: ST's installer gets SE_ERROR from the
first SE_Decrypt_Append of the verify pass while main() makes the same call
successfully, and 0003's trace shows SE_CRYPTO_Decrypt_Append is never
entered on the failing path -- so the guard is in the gate, and the two
callers differ only in where their buffers live (main() uses statics, ST's
loop uses stack).

GENERATED WITH diff, NOT BY HAND -- see
patches/0002-sfu_fwimg_no_swap-trace-verify-steps.patch for why.
scratchpad/mkpatch4.py regenerates this file and asserts every guard it
means to mark was found.

